From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not build the setuid-root helper on Windows

octphelper exists so that a privileged step can be split out of the GUI.
Windows has no setuid, and MSYS2 has no root to escalate to -- pacman writes
to an installation the invoking user already owns, which is why MSYS2 ships
no sudo and its installer sets no special permissions on the install folder.

Shimming it into compiling would produce a binary that is a fiction twice
over: it refuses to do anything unless geteuid() == 0, which can never hold,
and it locates processes by walking /proc, which does not exist here. So it
is not built, and the three startup checks that abort when the binary is
absent are skipped with it.

Not for upstream as-is: the parts that replace the helper's job on Windows
are still open.
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 4b0a450..4775a6f 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,7 +8,15 @@ set(CMAKE_RUNTIME_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}")
 
 option(USE_QTERMWIDGET6 "Build with qtermwidget6 instead of qtermwidget5" ON)
 
-add_subdirectory(helper)
+# octphelper is the setuid-root helper. Windows has no setuid, and MSYS2 has
+# no root to escalate to: pacman runs as the user who owns the installation.
+# The binary would also be a fiction -- it refuses to do anything unless
+# geteuid() == 0, and it finds processes by walking /proc, which does not
+# exist here. So it is not built rather than shimmed into something that
+# compiles and lies.
+if(NOT WIN32)
+  add_subdirectory(helper)
+endif()
 add_subdirectory(notifier)
 add_subdirectory(cachecleaner)
 add_subdirectory(repoeditor)
diff --git a/cachecleaner/main.cpp b/cachecleaner/main.cpp
index 4b7079d..a647c18 100644
--- a/cachecleaner/main.cpp
+++ b/cachecleaner/main.cpp
@@ -64,11 +64,16 @@ int main( int argc, char *argv[] )
     return (-3);
   }
 
+#ifndef Q_OS_WIN
+  // Not built on Windows; see the top-level CMakeLists. Requiring it
+  // here would abort every start for the sake of a binary that has
+  // nothing to do.
   if (!QFile::exists(ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH))
   {
     qDebug() << "Aborting cache-cleaner as 'octphelper' binary could not be found! [" << ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH << "]";
     return (-4);
   }
+#endif
 
   if (UnixCommand::findExecutable(ctn_QTSUDO).isEmpty())
   {
diff --git a/notifier/main.cpp b/notifier/main.cpp
index 075e202..e2d79ea 100644
--- a/notifier/main.cpp
+++ b/notifier/main.cpp
@@ -52,11 +52,16 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     return (-2);
   }
 
+#ifndef Q_OS_WIN
+  // Not built on Windows; see the top-level CMakeLists. Requiring it
+  // here would abort every start for the sake of a binary that has
+  // nothing to do.
   if (!QFile::exists(ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH))
   {
     qDebug() << "Aborting notifier as 'octphelper' binary could not be found! [" << ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH << "]";
     return (-3);
   }
+#endif
 
   if (UnixCommand::findExecutable(ctn_QTSUDO).isEmpty())
   {
diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index a1ba6dc..d814fdb 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -36,11 +36,16 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     return (-1);
   }
 
+#ifndef Q_OS_WIN
+  // Not built on Windows; see the top-level CMakeLists. Requiring it
+  // here would abort every start for the sake of a binary that has
+  // nothing to do.
   if (!QFile::exists(ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH))
   {
     qDebug() << "Aborting octopi as 'octphelper' binary could not be found! [" << ctn_OCTOPI_HELPER_PATH << "]";
     return (-2);
   }
+#endif
 
   if (UnixCommand::findExecutable(ctn_QTSUDO).isEmpty())
   {
